// Owned, but with no slot to run in: the roster outgrew `Game::pet_capacity`
// and this program is one of the newest past it. Slots are not a door any
// more — a capture past them succeeds — so this is what they cost instead.
//
// Harsh on purpose. At the strike cap it sits past `MORALE_LASHES_OUT_AT`
// (-75) even a full `MEMORY_POSTING_PERIOD` after its last strike, so a
// program left without a slot ends up brawling with no other grievance. The
// short half-life is the other half: build a Data Cache and it fades.
//
// `Nothing` as a subject, `ran_down`'s reason: no tile, machine or colleague
// is to blame for the player not having built the room.
(
    id: "unslotted",
    name: "Unslotted",
    blurb: "Had nowhere of its own to run.",
    valence: -22.0,
    half_life: 2000,
    subject: Nothing,
    strike_cap: 4,
)
